      "value": "@{5a3c5fa04a8da67427803b3e|full_name}:  I leave the proper in-game implementation up to the devs as they would know far better than I where UI options for this should fit in.  Given we can assume there would need to be a new UI menu added even to list the shaders active in a given world, or on players, I would assume just the same that options would be added to that new menu to block/unblock shaders.  \n\nI think its pretty easy to rail against this idea.  Easier still to attack others online while claiming to be better informed.. \n \nI appreciate any input that seeks to find better implementation methods for the idea in general.   The goal is not \"to kill vrchat creativity\" but to protect its community from abuses where possible.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
