      "value": "@{5a4b034d1ab4366d42644996|full_name}: I knew it used GUID for resources, just am not sure about how Shader.Find() method and the Editor decide which shader with name 'X' is the shader you wanted to operate on.  I'm assuming its either a FIFO where any others by the same name are either blocked OR they are examined for additional shader code to merge into one shader of the same name.. \n\nEither way, I think its right to assume blocking by name only would come with several gotchas.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
