      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be very difficult to implement. If you approach this by making it list all shaders in the lobby and letting users disable ones they don't want to see, this is already a major flaw with the idea. A crasher could rename his crash shader to 'flat lit toon' for example by opening its code and changing one line. In the list, people would think its just another toon shader and leave it unblocked. If, perhaps, they could figure out how to automatically block malicious shaders without a list that would be nice but also have its own set of problems. Shader makers constantly use new and interesting ways to make their shaders work, which means automatically detecting some things may be very difficult.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
