  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-08-13T04:55:26.743Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat could use a method to prevent undesired shader effects from being run.  Users should be able to add more shaders to a default list of whitelisted shaders either via a config file or an in-game menu that lists shaders by name. \n\nI think an option like this would help in a few ways, from potentially dealing with crashers, to providing a layer of protection for photosensitive players in VR.   With proper defaults in this shader whitelist configuration there would be little impact to character or world creation or existing data on genuine players.  The use of shaders would still be allowed, but users would have a choice of if they want to allow that code/effect, similar to the particle limiter. \n\nThank you for your consideration!",
  "error": null,
